extends RefCounted
## Tonight's case, for the Noir office's typewriter: a hundred and more of them, dealt out in a shuffled order so
## you don't see one twice until you've seen them all. Each is [title, the case, the closing line].
## {tux} and {calico} become the cats' names (whatever you've called them).

const CASES := [
	["THE VANISHING TREATS", "The treat bag was full at nine. By ten it was a sad paper ghost. {tux} was asleep on the bed with crumbs on her whiskers and an alibi nobody believed.", "Case closed. The bag was the only witness, and it wasn't talking."],
	["THE CARTRIDGE THAT KNEW TOO MUCH", "A cart turned up in the drawer that nobody remembered buying. No label, no prints. When I blew in it, the TV blinked twice, like it knew me.", "I put it back. Some games you don't play. Some games play you."],
	["A HIGH SCORE IN THE RAIN", "Somebody beat my score on the arcade at three in the morning. Three letters on the board: ???. The joystick was still warm.", "I didn't sleep. I practised. Tomorrow, I get my initials back."],
	["THE LAST SLICE", "One slice of pizza left in the box. I went to wash my hands. When I came back, the box was empty and the room was very, very quiet.", "I'll never know who. But I know {calico} won't look me in the eye."],
	["THE MISSING CONTROLLER", "Player two's controller was gone. The cable led under the beanbag and stopped, cut clean. Somebody didn't want to lose.", "I found it in the fridge, next to the sodas. Cold. Like the person who put it there."],
	["BLUE MOON OVER THE ARCADE", "The cabinet's screen glowed blue with nobody playing. INSERT COIN, it said, over and over, like a man who's had too many.", "I gave it a coin. It gave me peace. Fair trade."],
	["THE SAVE FILE", "Forty hours of a game, gone. The save slot said EMPTY in letters as cold as a landlord's handshake.", "Somebody pressed the wrong button. Somebody always does."],
	["THE STOLEN BEANBAG", "The pink beanbag moved two inches toward the TV overnight. Nobody admits to it. Beanbags don't walk. Usually.", "I marked its spot with tape. Let it try that again."],
	["SMOKE AND SAXOPHONES", "A saxophone was playing somewhere in the building. Every night at one. Nobody in the building owns a saxophone.", "I stopped asking. Some music you just let in."],
	["THE NAP THAT WENT TOO LONG", "I closed my eyes at eight. I opened them at four. The record had stopped, the rain hadn't, and my coffee had grown a personality.", "Nobody did it. That's the worst kind of case."],
	["THE DIARY'S LAST PAGE", "The diary on the nightstand was missing its last page. Torn neat, like someone knew exactly what was on it.", "I wrote it again from memory. It came out sadder."],
	["THE MAN WHO PRESSED START", "He walked in, pressed START on the console and walked out. Didn't play. Didn't say a word. The game's been waiting ever since.", "I let it wait. Patience is a virtue. So is minding your business."],
	["THE NEON THAT BLINKED", "The HOTEL sign across the street flickered in a pattern. Three short, three long, three short. Either a cry for help or a bad wire.", "I called the hotel. Bad wire. I was almost disappointed."],
	["A KAIJU WALKS INTO A CITY", "Something big walked past the window last night. The whole building hummed. The insurance people say it was 'weather'.", "Weather doesn't leave footprints the size of a bus."],
	["THE MONKEY ON THE SHELF", "The little King Gaboon on the bookshelf was facing the wall this morning. I didn't turn him. Nobody did.", "I turned him back. He looked relieved. So was I."],
	["THE SAUCER AT THE WINDOW", "Lights at the glass, a hum in my teeth, and a grey face looking in like it owed me money.", "It left before I could ask what it wanted. They always do."],
	["THE TAPE WITH NO LABEL", "A VHS tape on the doorstep. No label, no note. Forty minutes of static and one second of someone waving.", "I rewound it. I watched it again. I waved back."],
	["THE RECORD THAT SKIPPED", "Same song, same groove, same skip, every night at midnight. The needle's fine. The record's fine. The skip is not.", "Some songs want you to hear a line twice. I listened."],
	["THE COLD COFFEE", "Left a coffee on the desk. Came back and it was colder than a parking ticket and twice as bitter.", "Time did it. Time always does it. Can't arrest time."],
	["THE MISSING SOCK", "One sock, gone. The other one is in the drawer, waiting, like a widow at a window.", "I'll find it in a year, behind the dresser, with no explanation. They always come back."],
	["THE KNOCK AT ELEVEN", "Somebody knocked at the front door at eleven sharp. Nobody there. Just rain, and a wet footprint going nowhere.", "I left the porch light on. Whoever it was, they'll be back."],
	["THE PHONE THAT RANG ONCE", "The wall phone rang once and stopped. The screen said UNKNOWN in letters that looked tired.", "If it's important, they'll call again. If it's trouble, they'll come in person."],
	["THE FRIDGE IN THE GAME ROOM", "The sodas in the game room fridge rearranged themselves. Red, blue, yellow, every night. Like a code.", "I drank the code. Tasted like cherry."],
	["THE THEATER'S EMPTY SEAT", "Twelve seats. Eleven empty. One warm. Nobody had been in all evening.", "I sat in it. Good view. I see why they stayed."],
	["THE CASE OF THE WRONG CHANNEL", "The TV was on channel 3. I never leave it on channel 3. Channel 3 is where the news lives, and the news is never good.", "I turned it off. Some stories don't need telling twice."],
	["DOWN IN THE FOG", "The fog came up to the balcony rail last night, thick as a lawyer's excuse. Something moved in it. Something big and slow.", "I went back inside. Curiosity's a cat. So is {tux}, and she's smarter than me."],
	["THE PLANT THAT GREW", "The plant in the hallway grew a new leaf overnight. Healthy, green, pointing straight at the study.", "Plants know things. I watered it. Never hurts to have a friend."],
	["THE INCENSE CONFESSION", "The incense burned down to nothing and the smoke spelled a word on the ceiling. I didn't catch it. I was blinking.", "Next time I'll keep my eyes open. Probably."],
	["THE BLANKET ON THE COUCH", "The blanket on the couch was folded. I don't fold blankets. Nobody I know folds blankets.", "Somebody here has standards. I'm a little afraid of them."],
	["THE ELEVATOR THAT ISN'T", "This building has no elevator. Last night I heard one ding. Twice. Then a voice said 'twelfth floor'.", "We're on the top floor. I didn't check what was above us. I didn't want to know."],
	["THE MISSING HIGH NOTE", "The singer in my favourite song used to hit a high note at 2:14. Tonight she didn't. Same file. Same speakers.", "Maybe she was tired. We all get tired."],
	["THE CROOKED POSTER", "The poster on the wall was hanging crooked. One degree. I straightened it. An hour later: crooked again.", "It wants to be crooked. Who am I to say different?"],
	["THE DAME FROM 4B", "She came in from 4B wanting her umbrella back. I never borrowed an umbrella. She didn't believe me. Neither did the umbrella in my hall.", "I gave it back. Nicest thing that happened all week."],
	["THE LONG HELICOPTER NIGHT", "News helicopters circled the city all night. Searchlights on the rooftops, looking for something they never found.", "They never find it. That's how you know it's real."],
	["THE PIGEON WITH A GRUDGE", "Same pigeon on the balcony rail, every morning, staring. Not cooing. Staring.", "I put out a cracker. We have an understanding now."],
	["THE LATE CHECKOUT", "The bed was made. I didn't make it. The pillows were fluffed with a precision that felt like a threat.", "Somebody wants me to sleep well. I'm suspicious, but I'll take it."],
	["THE LOST REMOTE", "The remote was gone. Couch cushions: empty. Under the couch: a coin, a crayon and regret.", "It was in the fridge. Again. We need to talk about the fridge."],
	["THE GHOST IN THE MONITOR", "The PC woke up by itself at 2 am, played thirty seconds of a song, and went back to sleep. No updates. No reason.", "Even computers have dreams. I let it have this one."],
	["THE SECOND CAT", "Two cats, the vet says. I counted three tonight. The third one left before I could get a good look.", "{calico} knows who it was. {calico} isn't telling."],
	["THE WET UMBRELLA", "A wet umbrella in the stand, and it hadn't rained in a week. It was dripping on my good floor.", "I let it dry. Evidence is evidence, even when it's damp."],
	["THE BROKEN RECORD", "Somebody scratched my favourite record. One clean line, right across the chorus.", "I bought another one. The scratch is still the best part."],
	["THE CASE OF THE GREEN LAMP", "The banker's lamp on my desk turned itself off at midnight. I didn't touch it. The bulb was fine.", "It wanted to be dark for a minute. I understand. Me too."],
	["THE FIRE ESCAPE", "Footsteps on the fire escape at three. Slow, careful, going up. Nobody lives above us.", "In the morning there was a wet print on the roof hatch. I'm not going up there. Not yet."],
	["THE BIG SCREEN", "The theater played a movie I've never heard of. Black and white, no sound, a man at a desk just like this one, typing.", "I turned around to check the desk. Nobody there. I left the room quickly."],
	["THE DISAPPEARING DOORMAT", "The doormat said WELCOME on Monday. On Tuesday it said WELCOME BACK.", "I didn't go anywhere. Did I?"],
	["THE PIZZA THAT ARRIVED", "A pizza arrived. Nobody ordered it. The receipt said 'paid in full' and 'you'll need this'.", "I did need it. I ate the evidence."],
	["THE CLOCK THAT STOPPED", "The VCR clock blinked 12:00 again. I set it on Sunday. Something keeps resetting the time in this place.", "Maybe time doesn't want to be set. Maybe neither do I."],
	["THE TWO-PLAYER MYSTERY", "The console had a second player on the screen and only one controller plugged in. Player two was winning.", "I unplugged it. Player two kept winning. I went to bed."],
	["THE CITY THAT HUMMED", "At four in the morning the whole city went quiet, then hummed one long note, like a choir clearing its throat.", "Nobody else heard it. I'm writing it down so somebody did."],
	["THE MAN IN THE GREY HAT", "A grey man in a grey hat sat in my client chair and said nothing for an hour. Then he said 'thanks for the company' and left.", "Some cases are just company. That's fine. That's plenty."],
	["THE STEAMED-UP WINDOW", "Somebody wrote 'LOOK UP' in the fog on the bedroom window. From the outside.", "I looked up. Rooftops, rain, one red light blinking. Probably a plane. Probably."],
	["THE LIBRARY BOOK", "A comic on my shelf I never bought. Due back in 1987. The library closed in 1989.", "I'll keep it. Nobody's coming to collect. I hope."],
	["THE ROLLED-UP RUG", "The rolled-up rug in the living room was unrolled this morning. The boxes were unpacked. Nobody unpacked them.", "Somebody wanted me to feel at home. It worked. I'm still nervous."],
	["THE MISSING NIGHT", "My watch says I slept two hours. The sun says I slept ten. One of them is lying and I know which one wears a strap.", "I threw the watch in the drawer. The sun can stay."],
	["THE CRYING RADIATOR", "The radiator in the study cried all night. Little sobs, every twenty minutes. Plumber says it's air in the pipes.", "Plumbers don't believe in sad radiators. I bought it a cover. It seems better."],
	["THE WRONG NUMBER", "Somebody called asking for 'the detective'. I said wrong number. They said 'not for long' and hung up.", "I put my hat on. Just in case."],
	["THE GOLDFISH ALIBI", "The goldfish across the hall saw everything. Unfortunately, goldfish forget everything in three seconds.", "Best witness I ever had. Worst memory. Like me on a Friday."],
	["THE LIGHT UNDER THE DOOR", "There's a light under the study door at night. The study's empty. The lamp is off. The light is warm.", "I didn't open the door. Some lights you leave alone."],
	["THE SODA FIZZ", "Every can in the fridge was shaken. Every single one. Somebody's playing the long game.", "I opened them all over the sink. Victory tastes sticky."],
	["THE MISSING STAR", "There's a star I see every night from the balcony, just above the tallest tower. Tonight it wasn't there.", "Maybe it's on a break. Even stars need a night off."],
	["THE ARCADE GHOST", "A ghost of the last player shows on the arcade glass when the screen goes dark. Same face every time. Smiling.", "I leave it a coin on the ledge. You keep ghosts happy."],
	["THE CHAIR THAT TURNED", "The recliner was facing the window when I left. When I came back it was facing the door. Like it was waiting for someone.", "I sat in it facing the door. Nobody came. I'll try again tomorrow."],
	["THE MAIL THAT WASN'T", "A letter under the door with my name on it, written backwards. In a mirror it said 'stop reading this'.", "I stopped. Then I read it again. I'm a detective. It's a sickness."],
	["THE BAD MOVIE", "Somebody put a terrible movie in the theater VCR and then left. Two hours. No refunds.", "I watched it all. Some cases you solve by suffering."],
	["THE PURRING WALL", "There's a purr coming from inside the wall behind the bed. Both cats are accounted for.", "I knocked twice. It purred twice. We're friends now."],
	["THE MISSING CHAPTER", "The comic on the shelf skips from page 11 to page 14. The pages weren't torn out. They were never there.", "Somebody, somewhere, knows what happened on page 12. I envy them."],
	["THE NIGHT BUS", "A bus stopped below the balcony at 3 am. Nobody got on. Nobody got off. It waited a long time.", "Maybe it was waiting for me. I wasn't ready. Maybe next time."],
	["THE BROKEN UMBRELLA", "Found a broken umbrella on the balcony. We're on the top floor. It didn't fall from above. It came from below.", "The wind here is a liar. I'm keeping the umbrella."],
	["THE ICE IN THE GLASS", "The ice in my whiskey never melts. I've timed it. Three hours. Same cube.", "I'm not complaining. I'm just saying. Somebody look into that."],
	["THE STRANGE CART", "The cart on the floor in the game room says 'DO NOT INSERT' on the label in my handwriting. I don't remember writing it.", "I didn't insert it. Past me must have had a reason. Past me was smart, sometimes."],
	["THE SNOW IN SUMMER", "It snowed past the window for ten minutes in the middle of a warm night. Then it stopped like it was embarrassed.", "I didn't tell anybody. The weather has feelings too."],
	["THE GREY VISITOR'S QUESTION", "He asked me if the city ever sleeps. I said no. He said 'neither do we', and finished his drink.", "He didn't say who 'we' were. I didn't ask."],
	["THE STOLEN SPOTLIGHT", "A police helicopter's spotlight lit up my window for a full minute, then left. The cops say they weren't flying.", "Somebody wanted a better look at me. I hope they liked the hat."],
	["THE CASE OF THE TALL PLANT", "The tall plant in the bedroom corner is taller every night. An inch at a time. It's reaching for the lamp.", "I moved the lamp. It's reaching for me now. I'm getting a smaller plant."],
	["THE WRONG REFLECTION", "My reflection in the dark TV screen was wearing a different hat. A better hat, honestly.", "I'm going hat shopping tomorrow. Some clues are just advice."],
	["THE FOUR A.M. TOAST", "I heard a toaster pop at four in the morning. We don't own a toaster.", "There was toast on the counter. Buttered. I ate it. Case closed, crumbs everywhere."],
	["THE LOCKED DOOR", "The study door was locked from the inside. The study was empty. The key was in my pocket.", "I unlocked it. The chair was still spinning. I locked it again."],
	["THE SAD SAXOPHONE", "The record I put on was a happy one. It came out of the speakers sad. Same notes. Different heart.", "The record player knows my mood better than I do. That's a problem."],
	["THE MISSING RECEIPT", "A receipt for one fedora, one trench coat and one bottle of rye, dated tomorrow.", "I'll be busy tomorrow, it seems. I'd better rest up."],
	["THE KAIJU'S TOOTH", "Found a tooth on the balcony the size of my arm. White, cold, with frost on it.", "I put it on the shelf next to the figures. It looks right at home. That's what worries me."],
	["THE FLICKERING STREETLAMP", "The streetlamp below has flickered every night for a year. Tonight it was steady. Somebody fixed it, and nobody fixes anything.", "Something's changed down there. I'll keep an eye on it."],
	["THE BACKWARDS SONG", "One of the songs in the music folder plays backwards on Tuesdays. The rest of the week it's fine.", "I listen on Tuesdays now. It says nice things backwards."],
	["THE CAT ON THE CONSOLE", "{calico} sleeps on the game console every night. It's warm, sure. But she always faces the cartridge slot.", "She's guarding something. I've decided not to know what."],
	["THE CASE OF THE EXTRA STEP", "The theater has three steps down. Last night I counted four.", "In the morning: three. I'm not counting again."],
	["THE DUSTY FOOTPRINT", "One dusty footprint in the middle of the hallway rug. Bare, long, with too few toes.", "I didn't vacuum it. Evidence. And honestly, a little bit of art."],
	["THE BROKEN NEON", "The INSERT COIN neon lost its N. Now it says I SERT COIN. Nobody will tell me where the N went.", "I SERT COIN anyway. Old habits."],
	["THE BAD LUCK PENNY", "Found a penny on the doormat, heads down. Every time I flip it over, it's heads down again.", "Some coins just don't want to look at you. I get it."],
	["THE TELEGRAM", "A telegram, in this day and age. It said: STOP WORRYING STOP. That's all.", "I tried. I stopped for almost an hour. Personal best."],
	["THE MISSING ARMCHAIR", "The reading chair in the study moved a foot to the left. The rug moved with it. The floor didn't.", "Furniture in this place has opinions. I respect that."],
	["THE TIRED LANDLORD", "The landlord came by to fix the sink. He fixed three things that weren't broken and left the sink.", "The sink and I have accepted each other. Drip, drip. It's company."],
	["THE BLUE SCREEN", "Every TV in the apartment went blue at once and said CH 3. Then back to normal. Nobody touched a remote.", "Somebody was broadcasting. I wish they'd said something."],
	["THE MOTH", "A moth circled the green lamp all night like it had something to confess.", "It never did. Some witnesses just want the light."],
	["THE WALK-IN STRANGER", "A stranger walked in, sat in my client chair, said 'wrong office', and walked back out. There's only one office.", "He'll find the right one. Or it'll find him."],
	["THE SPILLED INK", "Ink spilled across my case file in the shape of the city skyline. Every tower. Even mine.", "I framed it. Best map I've ever had."],
	["THE QUIET RAIN", "For one minute the rain made no sound. Still falling, still wet, totally silent.", "Then it came back, louder, like it was sorry. I forgave it."],
	["THE TWO TOOTHBRUSHES", "Two toothbrushes in the cup. I live alone. One of them is grey.", "I'm not touching it. Hygiene is hygiene, mystery or not."],
	["THE ELEVENTH HOUR", "It was eleven. Then it was eleven again. The clock didn't move, the rain did.", "I lived that hour twice. The second one was better."],
	["THE MISSING FIGURE", "One of the little figures on the bookshelf went missing for a day. When it came back, it had a tiny scuff on its foot.", "It went somewhere. I hope it had a good time."],
	["THE UNSIGNED PAINTING", "The sunset print in the living room has a new tiny figure on the hill. Waving.", "I wave back now. It's polite. I'm told it's polite."],
	["THE BURNT TOAST CODE", "Somebody burned toast in the kitchen in a perfect circle. Three slices. Like a traffic light with no colour.", "I don't know what it means. I'm eating it anyway. Waste not."],
	["THE LONG GOODBYE", "My client said goodbye at the door and didn't leave for forty minutes. We talked about the rain the whole time.", "Best conversation I've had all year. Case closed. Heart open."],
	["THE BALCONY CHAIR", "One of the two balcony chairs is always wet, even when it doesn't rain. The other is always dry.", "I sit in the dry one. The wet one belongs to somebody. I let them have it."],
	["THE OVERDUE TAPE", "The video store called. I owe them for a tape I returned in 1994. The fine is $4,000.", "I'm going to need a bigger case. And a lawyer."],
	["THE SLEEPING DETECTIVE", "I woke up at my desk with a case already typed. Signed with my name. I don't remember writing it.", "It was a good case. Better than mine. I'm taking credit."],
	["THE SECRET BOOK", "There's a red book on the study shelf that sticks out further every night. Like it wants to be pulled.", "I know where it goes. You know where it goes. Let's keep it between us."],
	["THE WHISTLING KETTLE", "The kettle whistled a tune I know but can't name. Four notes, then silence.", "I hummed the rest. The kettle seemed satisfied."],
	["THE TOP FLOOR", "Somebody asked me which floor I live on. I said the top. They laughed for a long time.", "I checked the roof hatch. Locked. From the other side."],
]


static func count() -> int:
	return CASES.size()
